# The Vercel deployment is the MCP endpoint and nothing else — the website is on
# GitHub Pages, and `/` here redirects there. So everything the website needs and
# the function does not stays out of the upload.
#
# Every pattern is anchored with a leading slash. Without one, gitignore syntax
# matches at any depth: a bare `tools/` also excludes `mcp/src/tools/`, which
# deploys a server whose own tool modules are missing and fails in `tsc` rather
# than anywhere useful. CI checks out from git and never reads this file, so it
# cannot catch that for you.
/packs/
/data/
/assets/
/tools/
/.github/
/.cache/
/*.html
/mcp/node_modules/
/mcp/dist/
/mcp/*.tgz
